{#-
  X1 (Batch X, 2026-09-27): ONE "How a cost gets uncosted" block, rendered
  IDENTICALLY on /about/ and /movement/ from ONE set of words in
  _data/uncosted.js. (V12 shared the format and kept two sets of words; the
  /movement/ variant is retired.)

  The format is /about/'s: the heading block (metalabel + headline) and the
  step list are bands in their own right — direct children of <main> on both
  pages — and the step list is a full-bleed band body, unframed under D3. The
  closing line sits inside the step list, under the last step, so the list and
  its conclusion are one band body. `.u-2` on the last step is the export's.

  block(u, screenLabel)
    u            { label, heading, steps: [{label, text}], close }
    screenLabel  data-screen-label for the heading block
-#}
{%- macro block(u, screenLabel) -%}
<div class="seqhd"{% if screenLabel %} data-screen-label="{{ screenLabel }}"{% endif %}><div class="u-3 metalabel">{{ u.label | safe }}</div><h2 class="u-4">{{ u.heading | safe }}</h2></div>
<div>
{%- for s in u.steps %}
  <div class="{% if loop.last %}u-2 {% endif %}step"><div class="num">{{ loop.index }}</div><div><h3>{{ s.label | safe }}</h3><p>{{ s.text | safe }}</p></div></div>
{%- endfor %}
{%- if u.close %}
  <p class="uncosted-close">{{ u.close | safe }}</p>
{%- endif %}
</div>
{%- endmacro %}
